#Default Player Ship
  $Name: T-65c X-wing
#End

#Engine Wash Info

  ;; NOTE:  The default MUST be the first entry in the list of engine wash info

  ;; Engine wash code
  ;; max_wash_dist = MAX(ewp->length, bank->points[j].radius * ewp->radius_mult);
  ;; So just make one engine wash style with length of 100 and radius multiplier of some amount?
  ;; Does not work with ships with lots of little thrusters making up 1 engine
  ;; but those ships are small enough that 150 min should work
  ;; So list them out the manual way
  ;; ISD big thruster radius is ~45 so 45 * x = 300 -> x = ~6.5

  $Name: Default
  $Angle: 10.0
  $Radius Mult: 6.5
  $Length: 150
  $Intensity: 0.025

#End


#Ship Templates

;; Stats/value changes are all listed in Ship Templates
;; Visual/cosmetic changes are listed in Ship Classes

;; Notes on Stats:
  ; Recall, accel and decel are 0 to ~63% max speed, not full, so there is still some momentum feel.
	; We have a low deceleartion that are around 2 to allow small AI to slow down more quickly so they stop running into things,
  ;   and allow player to more easily slow down too 
  ;   (b/c if player dumps all power to engines they can get a really rapid slowdown to shake tails).
  ;   Also b/c cutting power should make you stop somewhat quickly in WW2 plane setting...?

  ; Recall, AI needs to be able to YAW well enough, since they are not smart enough to use faster roll.
  ; Also, normal players kinda of expect the yaw to do something, so keep it decent.
  ; And, faster roll does mean you can actually shake a tail though, since you are kinda out flying the AI.

  ; Also recall that engine script in missions-sct apply to player physics.
  ; The includes: 
  ;   "ForwardAccelerationTime", "ForwardDecelerationTime", 
  ;   "RotationalVelocityMax", 
  ;   "RotationalVelocityDamping", and "VelocityDamping"
  ; Note, RotationalVelocityMax is the tabled rotational times (AI actually uses these)

  ; Also recall that GCW does some more debufs to hostile ships, 
  ;   but due to the if conditions these don't really overlap.

;;======Common Templates======

;; --#TODO- Damage spews radii are locked at defaults until auto culling in FSO is added
;; b/c having smoke fill screen kills FPS

; Regarding "intrinsic no shields"... 
;;  we need to leave this setting on as there is logic in FSO which dictates that shield flag setting,
;;  which ensures that if the player switches to a ship with shields the shields will actually be on. 

$Template:	Common Ship Template
  ;$Selection Effect:			      OFF
  $Damage Lightning Type:       none
  $Impact:                      
    +Damage Type:               Collision_Damage_Low ;; AI can be dumb, player will use Collision_Damage_High via script on higher diffs
  $Impact Spew Effect:          PE_Empty
  $Damage Spew Effect:          PE_Empty
  $Gravity Const:               0.0
  $Dying Gravity Const:         1.0
  $Density:                     1
  $Banking Constant:            0.5
  $Slide Accel:                 0.0
  $Slide Decel:                 0.0
  $Glide:                       NO
  $Warpin type:                 Hyperspace
  $Warpin Start Sound:		      127
  $Warpin time:                 4.0
  $Warpin decel exp:            10.0
  $Warpout type:                Hyperspace
  $Warpout engage time:         2.0 ;change for S-foil ships with long rotation times
  $Warpout Speed:               1.0
  $Warpout time:                6.0
  $Warpout accel exp:           1.5
  $Expl inner rad:              10.0
  $Expl outer rad:              50.0
  $Expl damage:                 5.0
  $Expl blast:                  500.0
  $Expl Propagates:             YES
  $Expl Splits Ship:            NO
  $Expl Visual Rad:             1.0
  $Death Roll Explosion Effect: PE_Empty
  $Death FX Explosion Effect:   PE_Empty
  $Ship Splitting Particles:
    +Max Particles:             0
    +Min Particles:             0
  $Ship Death Effect:           PE_Empty
  $Debris Death Effect:         PE_Explosion_Asteroid
  $Shockwave Speed:             0 ; 0 = no shockwave
  $Shockwave Count:             0
  $Explosion Animations:        (10)
  $Shield Color:                100, 100, 100
  $Shield Impact Explosion:     none
  $Power Output:                1.0 ;`$ETS uses ship class power output:` flag enabled, this will act as a multiplier for ETS energy.
  $Countermeasures:             0 ;;0 for most ships except specific TIEs (using countermeasures as TIE special abilities)
  $Default Subsystem Death Effect: PE_Empty


$Template:	Common Fighter Template 
