$Template:	B-wing Template
  ; Needs MG9, not MG7-A
  +Use Template:                Rebel Fighter Template
  $Display Name:                B-wing Starfighter
  $Short name:                  B-wing
  $Species:                     Rebel
    +Type:                     XSTR("Bomber", 826) ; (Strategic Assault)
    +Maneuverability:          XSTR("Very Low", 827) ;;_1
    +Armor:                    XSTR("Heavy", 828) ;;_5
    +Manufacturer:             XSTR("Slayn and Korpil", 829)
    +Description:              XSTR(" ", 817)
    $end_multi_text
    +Tech Title:               XSTR("A/SF-01 B-wing Starfighter", 830)
    +Tech Description:         XSTR("Slayn & Korpil's B-wing starfighter is a heavily armed and armored assault platform developed during the Galactic Civil War by the Rebel Alliance.  Designed as part of the top-secret Project Shantipole by then-Commander Ackbar and a team of Verpine engineers, the A/SF-01 B-wing was a response to the Empire's increased deployment of escort frigates and other anti-starfighter vessels that were emerging at the time.

  Although the new bomber was intended to completely replace the aging Y-wing, the B-wing's adoption was slowed both by cost considerations and the difficulty that many pilots had in mastering the craft's unusual design and rotating cockpit module.  In spite of these drawbacks, the B-wing has proven itself to be a true powerhouse against capital ships--with each fighter carrying multiple ion cannons, a state-of-the-art heavy laser cannon, and two separate torpedo banks capable of delivering varied ordnance for a range of tactical conditions.  

  While the B-wing's dogfight performance is poor, its numerous weapon mounts allow its pilots to equip specialized anti-fighter weapons where necessary--or devote their three cannon banks to nothing but anti-capital weapons, if adequate escort is expected.  But a balanced loadout gives the craft excellent in-mission adaptability, which has proven the deciding factor in multiple engagements.  Properly equipped, a squadron of B-wings can reliably drive off or destroy targets as large as Imperial frigates.", 831)
    $end_multi_text
    +Length:                   17 m
    +Gun Mounts:               3
    +Missile Banks:            2

  $Cockpit POF file:	B-wing_cockpit.pof
