$Template:	TIE Interceptor 2 Template
  ;; debug complains about bank number mismatch if we try and use TIE Interceptor Template
  +Use Template:                Empire Fighter Template
  $Display Name:                TIE Interceptor (II)
  $Short name:                  TInterceptor2
  $Species:                     Imperial
    +Type:                     XSTR("Interceptor", 820)
    +Maneuverability:          XSTR("Excellent", 821) ;;_5
    +Armor:                    XSTR("Very Light", 839) ;;_1
    +Manufacturer:             XSTR("Sienar Fleet Systems", 840)
    +Description:              XSTR(" ", 817)
    $end_multi_text
    +Tech Title:               XSTR("TIE/in Interceptor Mark 2", 851)
    +Tech Description:         XSTR("Though loved by its pilots, the new TIE Interceptor was not without its problems.  Most prominently, many aces transitioning to the new class found that they preferred the standard fighter's chin-mounted laser cannons to the Interceptor's wingtip mounts for precision aiming.  While the L-s9.3 laser cannon was built for the chin position slot, the Interceptor did not have sufficient power to maintain a full rate of fire for six laser cannons, even with all power being directed to the weapons.  The solution to this problem was replacing the wingtip lasers with blaster cannons, short ranged rapid-fire weapons that are considered to be somewhat inaccurate in any position.  Updating the chin-mounted lasers also improved the modularity of the weapons systems, which allows the Mk. 2 to be equipped with the L-s8.1 ion cannon.  Officially, this new Mk.2 configuration is specially tuned to attack static targets (and the modified wing-tip cannons do make it extremely deadly in an antipersonnel/disabling role), but in practice some top squadrons fly the Mk.2 regardless of the mission profile.", 852)
    $end_multi_text
    +Length:                   10 m
    +Gun Mounts:               2
    +Missile Banks:            0

