$Template:	ARC-170 Template ;fighter/bomber
  +Use Template:                Rebel Fighter Template
  $Display Name:                ARC-170 Starfighter
  $Short name:                  ARC170
  $Species:                     Republic
    +Type:                     XSTR("Fighter/Bomber", 870)
    +Maneuverability:          XSTR("Average", 833) ;;_3
    +Armor:                    XSTR("Good", 814) ;;_4
    +Manufacturer:             XSTR("Incom Corporation", 816)
    +Description:              XSTR(" ", 817)
    $end_multi_text
    +Tech Title:               XSTR("ARC-170 Starfighter", 871)
    +Tech Description:         XSTR("A predecessor of the T-65 X-wing line, the Aggressive ReConnaissance (ARC)-170 Starfighter was developed during the final year of the Clone Wars as a heavy-hitting space superiority fighter for the Republic.  By this point, the war had spread to the far reaches of the Outer Rim, and the Republic was in need of a starfighter which could threaten Separatist capital ships while being maneuverable enough that it would not require a constant escort of dedicated space-superiority fighters.  Incom began development by improving the firepower of the Z-95, but ultimately had to make major structural changes to the fuselage and engines to account for the heavier weapons.  Testing revealed that the maneuverability remained less than ideal for evading nimble Separatist starfighters, so a defense turret was mounted to the rear of the fuselage.  Additionally, S-foil wings were added to disperse weapon-generated heat and improve coverage of the upgraded shielding.  

  The finished design possessed similar firepower to the BTL-A4 while being more maneuverable and far less vulnerable to enemy fighters.  Armed with a pair of heavy laser cannons, one torpedo bay, one bomb bay, and a rear turret, the ARC-170 became the fighter of choice for many squadrons within the Republic fleet.  The most noticeable downside, at least in the eyes of Republic Command, was that the range of weapons required a crew of three--a pilot, bombardier, and tail gunner.  

  After the Clone Wars, the ARC-170 was decommissioned in favor of single-pilot fighters.  Most ARCs were sent to scrap processing centers, though many ships were discreetly sold to third-party vendors, then retrofitted for use in privateer and bounty hunting work.  As a benefit, the ARC-170's large capacitors and powerful reactor permit the use of laser cannons typically reserved for much larger attack craft.  The bulky rangefinders mounted above the heavy guns were rendered obsolete some years after the war by improving sensor technology, so privte owners often replace them with ion cannons or other weapons to improve offensive flexibility.  Other common aftermarket modifications include wiring bomb controls to the pilot and installing a droid control for the rear turret, while replacing the freed-up crew spaces with advanced navigational capabilities and additional cargo space for prolonged journeys.  ", 872)
    $end_multi_text
    +Length:                   12.7 m
    +Gun Mounts:               2
    +Missile Banks:            2

  $Cockpit POF file:	ARC170_cockpit.pof
