$Template:	TYE-Vulture Template ;Pirate half way between Y-wing and X-wing, 4 fire points in 1 bank, can also equip ions but has no secondaries
  +Use Template:                Common Fighter Template
  $Display Name:                TYE-Vulture Raider
  $Short name:                  TYE-Vulture
  $Species:                     Pirate
    +Type:                     XSTR("Fighter", 813)
    +Maneuverability:          XSTR("Low", 858) ;;_2
    +Armor:                    XSTR("Heavy", 828) ;;_4
    +Manufacturer:             XSTR("Various", 867)
    +Description:              XSTR(" ", 817)
    $end_multi_text
    +Tech Title:               XSTR("TYE-Vulture Raider", 882)
    +Tech Description:         XSTR("Among the more effective ugly builds are those created for a single very specific purpose.  One such model is the TYE-Vulture, a design dedicated solely to commerce raiding.  Like the TYE-wing, the Vulture is built around a TIE Starfighter that has been retired due to irreparable engine failure.  In addition to a pair of familiar R200 engines, sturdy Chempat shields are added along with a Novaldex power generator.  This allows the smaller cockpit reactor to deliver power exclusively to weapons, which usually consist of two pairs of T&B IX4 laser cannons and a chin-mounted L-s8.1 ion cannon.  With both reactors running, the radiator arrays from the original TIE are required to dissipate heat at an acceptable rate, and are generally placed around the hull where they can offer a measure of protection from high angle deflection shots.  Because of this ramshackle arrangement of parts, the Vulture's poor handling characteristics are a given, though it does boast a slightly higher speed than the Y-wing, allowing it to close on its prey quickly and shrug off multiple shots before delivering a crippling barrage.

  It should be noted that the non-TIE parts of this design are almost always acquired individually rather than being salvaged from a Y-wing.  The popularity of Koensayr's fighter-bombers makes the aftermarket components used in the Vulture more affordable and ensures their compatibility, but no sane sentient would ever waste a perfectly good Y-wing hull to create an inferior ship.  Contrary to popular belief, this is the case for the majority of ugly designs.  While many one-of-a-kind creations do exist that are the result of freakish attempts to meld two distinct ships into one, uglies are usually attempts to salvage a single non-functional ship as cheaply as possible.  The TYE-Vulture is somewhat unique in that regard because, for the cost of all the added parts, a buyer could simply purchase a new engine for the TIE and save a great deal of time and effort.  This is not as tempting an option for potential Vulture operators as it seems, however, as any group interested in a fighter whose sole use is raiding is unlikely to have access to the sort of equipment and expertise required to maintain a twin ion engine.", 883)
    $end_multi_text
    +Length:                   10 m
    +Gun Mounts:               2
    +Missile Banks:            0

