$Template:	ZTI-wing Template ;Pirate interceptor attempt at upgrade, rolls better than Z95 but less secondaries, 4 fire points in 1 bank
  +Use Template:                Common Fighter Template
  $Display Name:                ZTI-wing Headhunter
  $Short name:                  ZTI-wing
  $Species:                     Pirate
    +Type:                     XSTR("Fighter", 813)
    +Maneuverability:          XSTR("Good", 814) ;;_4
    +Armor:                    XSTR("Light", 822) ;;_2
    +Manufacturer:             XSTR("Various", 867)
    +Description:              XSTR(" ", 817)
    $end_multi_text
    +Tech Title:               XSTR("ZTI-wing Headhunter", 884)
    +Tech Description:         XSTR("Colloquially called the Zeety, the ZTI-wing represents one of the more successful attempts to upgrade the firepower of the base Headhunter with newer Imperial technology.  As the TIE/in Interceptor came into wide use by the Empire and damaged or defective ships began appearing in scrapyards across the Galaxy, entrepreneurial engineers acquired these components through various channels and began experimenting with new iterations of uglies.

  The Zeety boasts double the primary firepower of the base Z-95 due to the four wing-mounted L-s9.3 laser cannons, albeit with a slightly slower acceleration due to the extra mass of the four wings.  Given its greater age, the base Z-95 fuselage lacked the advanced cooling systems of Imperial TIEs, so retrofitted cooling couplings were rigged up in the easiest accessible area--the missile bay.  As a result, the Zeety has only half the warhead capacity compared to the base Z-95.  Still, the augmented primary firepower of this ugly has often proved the deciding factor for success in hit-and-run operations.", 885)
    $end_multi_text
    +Length:                   12 m
    +Gun Mounts:               1
    +Missile Banks:            1

