$Template:	TBlade Bomber Template ;Pirate bomber like the B-wing
  ; Needs MG9, not MG7-A
  +Use Template:                Common Fighter Template
  $Display Name:                T-Blade Bomber
  $Short name:                  TBlade
  $Species:                     Pirate
    +Type:                     XSTR("Bomber", 826)
    +Maneuverability:          XSTR("Very Low", 827) ;;_1
    +Armor:                    XSTR("Heavy", 828) ;;_5
    +Manufacturer:             XSTR("Various", 867)
    +Description:              XSTR(" ", 817)
    $end_multi_text
    +Tech Title:               XSTR("T-Blade Bomber", 886)
    +Tech Description:         XSTR("One of the most recent uglies, the T-Blade is one of the heaviest hitting private bombers.  For many years the Y-wing was the bomber of choice for illegal operations.  The Rebels' A/SF-01 B-wing is a new and sophisticated craft, and not produced in nearly the numbers required for widespread secondhand access--but it is also complex and highly demanding of maintenance, and the Alliance quickly found that production of spare parts in large quantities was a must.  The Alliance's status as a resistance organization meant that much of their logistics were done through independent smugglers, and some of those smugglers chose to skim a few B-wing parts off the top and see what could be done with them.

  It was discovered that attaching TIE/sa Bomber wings to the B-wing fuselage was far easier and cheaper than acquiring and attaching more complex moving S-foils.  Corner cutting resulted in less primary firepower compared to the base B-wing, but the addition of radiating wings allowed for slightly better energy dispersal and marginally improved handling.  Integrating these components into the central fuselage also required unifying the separate warhead launchers possessed by the original B-wing model.  Equipping only one warhead type at a time, but with higher volume, is an ability that pilots tend to appreciate or resent depending on how well their current mission is going.  Notwithstanding debate, the T-Blade's indisputable heavy firepower allows it to serve effectively in a heavy attack role for private operations.  ", 887)
    $end_multi_text
    +Length:                   17 m
    +Gun Mounts:               3
    +Missile Banks:            1

