$Template:	ATAT #Base Template
  +Use Template:                Common Transport Template
  $Display Name:                AT-AT
  $Short name:                  ATAT
  $Species:                     Imperial
  +Tech Title:                  XSTR("All Terrain Armored Transport", 934)
  +Tech Description:
  XSTR("Officially designated as the All Terrain Armored Transport, this imposing four-legged walker is as durable as it is terrifying to anyone unlucky enough to be caught in its path.  Developed for devastating firepower and maximum versatility, the first iterations of these vehicles were deployed early in the Empire's expansion to effectively restore order to chaotic population centers across the Mid and Outer Rim.  Continued use and field reports fueled an iterative process that resulted in the current generation of AT-ATs, which are now universally recognized as symbols of Imperial supremacy on almost any planetary or lunar terrain.

  In addition to transporting a full platoon of Imperial stormtroopers into battle, each AT-AT effectively serves as a fortified, mobile command post capable of repositioning as needed during combat situations.  Though not designed for speed, the optimized mechanical frame and specially-tuned drive motors support nearly impenetrable cruiser-grade armor that far outclasses most that of ground vehicles, rendering the hull virtually impervious to even heavy blasters.  Meanwhile, the heavy chin cannons and versatile temple blasters can easily neutralize even large targets with a single barrage.

  Since the AT-AT concentrates its firepower forward, Imperial Command has found that deploying these behemoth walkers in small, staggered squads or with additional smaller support vehicles can help cover their flanks and rear during ground assaults.  The potency of the AT-AT also makes it one of the few ground vehicles to be occasionally positioned on larger orbital installations, either to improve defensive firepower or support boarding operations.", 935)
  $end_multi_text

  $Damp:                 		  0.0 ;
  $Rotdamp:               	  1.0 ; big ship rot damp
