$Template:	c70 Template
  ;; less agile/accl but slightly tougher hull and slightly weaker shields, also long turrets
  +Use Template:                Common Frigate Template
  $Display Name:                Charger c70 Frigate
  $Short name:                  c70
  $Species:                     Republic
  +Tech Title:                  XSTR("Charger c70 Frigate", 944)
  +Tech Description:
  XSTR("The 'Charger c70' retrofit of the Consular-class cruiser likely inspired the common practice of deploying militarized Corellian corvettes in combat roles.  Developed over three decades before the Clone Wars, the original Consular-class cruiser was originally used in civilian transport roles, and achieved particular status when the Republic Diplomatic Corps adopted it as an ambassadorial transport.  When the Clone Wars erupted, the Republic Navy--stretched thin and working with a very limited fleet--quickly set about modifying their existing Consulars for combat use.  With additional armor and multiple turbolaser batteries, and overclocked drives that gave the ship remarkable agility even despite the extra load, the class was redesignated as a light frigate.  The retrofit saw great battlefield success in skirmishing and escort roles, and the Corellian Engineering Corporation was able to secure a contract to mass-produce the modified version.  The considerable profits helped fund the development of the later CR90 corvette, which would come to see even greater popularity than the Charger in the following decades.  

  Although only one hundred and fifty meters in length, the Charger c70 boasts six long-range turbolasers that provide nearly omnidirectional coverage.  This heavy armament, combined with the vessel's small size and high speed, makes the Charger extremely dangerous to larger ships.  However, the frigate's lack of point defenses leaves it vulnerable to fighter attack unless escort is provided.  Mainly used by private organizations in recent years, the Charger c70 frigate remains a capable ship that can deliver capital-grade firepower at a low cost.", 945)
  $end_multi_text
