$Template:	Raider Template
  +Use Template:                Common Frigate Template
  $Display Name:                Raider Corvette
  $Short name:                  Raider
  $Species:                     Imperial
  +Tech Title:                  XSTR("Raider-class Corvette", 946)
  +Tech Description:
  XSTR("While not as imposing as most Imperial warships, the Raider-class Corvette represents the latest advances in naval research and design.  For many years, the Imperial navy used CR90 Corvettes and retrofitted Gozanti-class Transports as patrol craft and escorts, but it gradually became clear to fleet officers that those decades-old ships--whose preexisting popularity with civilian spacers meant their design shortcomings were uncomfortably common knowledge--were less-than-ideal workhorses for the growing Imperial war machine.  Following its developing fleet doctrine, the Imperial Navy commissioned Kuat to design a modern corvette-class vessel more capable than any other ship of its size.

  Centered around a powerful engine system and robust armament, the Raider has found a niche as a special-operations vessel.  Elongated cooling conduits of the engine blocks and concentrated power couplers span over half of the ship length, providing the fastest acceleration of any warship in the Imperial Starfleet.  This speed, coupled with the high firepower-to-length ratio, allows the Raider to launch into a hostile zone quickly while providing a defensive firing screen--often with the goal of extracting special force operatives using the main hangar bay or external TIE dock tubes.  The compact size allows the vessel to deploy rapidly and flexibly, although its lack of volume does present key vulnerabilities against determined and well-equipped starfighters or larger warships.  As such, the most efficient use of the Raider is to leverage its engine speed, either in support of large fleet operations where fighter cover is available or to perform fast extractions from combat zones before hostiles can inflict any serious damage.", 947)
  $end_multi_text
  $POF file:           		  raider.pof
  $POF target LOD:              0
  $Detail distance:       	  (0, 1700, 5000)
  $Collision LOD:               1
  $Damp:                 		  0.6 ; big ship damp
  $Rotdamp:               	  1.0 ; big ship rot damp
  $Max Velocity:          	  0.0, 5.0, 100.0 ;big ship speed velocity vector (needs y speed to dock)
  $Rotation time:               40, 46, 34
  $Rear Velocity:               0.0
  $Forward accel:               20.0 ;big ship accel
  $Forward decel:               0.0 ;big ship decel, follows wp to move
  $Ship Death Effect:           PE_Explosion_Ship_Big_Imperial
  $Default PBanks:        	  ()
  $Default SBanks:        	  ()
  $SBank Capacity:       		  ()
  $Shields:               	  6000 
    ;+Auto Spread: 15
    ;+Spread From LOD: 2
  $Shield Regeneration Rate:    0.00 ;captial ship shield regen
  +Shield Regen Hit Delay:      4.0  ;captial ship shield delay
  $Max Oclk Speed:        	  100.0 ;big ship velocity max speed
  $Max Weapon Eng:        	  100.0
  $Hitpoints:             	  18800
  $Hull Repair Rate:            0.0
  $Subsystem Repair Rate:       0.0
  $Armor Type:				          Capital_Hull_Armor
  $Shield Armor Type:           Capital_Shield_Armor
  $Flags:         			        ( "large ship deathroll" "cruiser" "model point shields" "disable all generic impact debris" "disable all generic explosion debris" "no ets" ) 
  $AI Class:             		    AI_07_Captain
  $Afterburner:          		    NO
  $Scan time:                   4500
  $EngineSnd:       			      208
  $Minimum Engine Volume:       0.3
  $Flyby Sound: 				        157
  $Closeup_pos:           	    0.0, 0.0, -160
  $Closeup_zoom:          	    0.5
  $Closeup_pos_targetbox:       0.0, 0.0, -600
  $Closeup_zoom_targetbox:      0.2
