$Template:	Arquitens #I Template
  +Use Template:                Common CruiserSmall Template
  $Display Name:                Arquitens Cruiser
  $Short name:                  Arquitens (Imp)
  $Species:                     Imperial
  +Tech Title:                  XSTR("Arquitens-class Light Cruiser", 952)
  +Tech Description:
  XSTR("Engineered and produced by Kuat Drive Yards, the Arquitens-class light cruiser has proven to be a capable and effective warship for its three-hundred-fifty meter size.  The Arquitens was originally deployed by the Republic during the Clone Wars, where it was designed to outflank and destroy the Separatists' potent but fragile Recusant artillery ships.  Outside of fleet engagements, the Arquitens commonly served as an escort for the larger Venator-class, or a guard for remote outposts.  Following the rise of the New Order, the Arquitens was one of the few warships to continue serving in the Imperial Navy without heavy modification, which is a testament to the original design.  Critically, the hangar bay, which previously could not hold the large Republic starfighters, proved sizable enough to hold and launch the new TIE Starfighters with only minimal modification.

  Within the Imperial Navy, the Arquitens serves in multiple support and rapid response roles.  The turbolaser configuration is optimized to focus fire onto a single forward target, and the main guns have considerable range, so a common battle strategy is to concentrate fire on soft targets at the rear of the enemy line.  Given the small number of heavy guns, the Arquitens can be disarmed by well-targeted starfighter attacks; accordingly, a fighter escort is typically assigned to the vessel.  The ability to launch an entire TIE squadron from such a small, well-armed ship provides a distinct benefit compared to similarly sized Imperial vessels such as the Carrack-class, which can only support up to four docked TIE craft.  The internal hangar bay also supports launching small troop transports, though the volume is not able to accommodate larger ground assault hardware such as Imperial walkers.  Though a less modern design compared to other light cruisers, the Arquitens continues to receive support and new orders ensuring it will continue to be a common sight in of the Imperial Fleet.", 953)
  $end_multi_text
  $POF file:                    arquitens.pof
  $POF target LOD:              0
  $Detail distance:             (0, 1500, 3000, 8000)
  $Collision LOD:				1
  $Damp:                        0.6 ; big ship damp
  $Rotdamp:                     1.0 ; big ship rot damp
  $Max Velocity:                0.0, 5.0, 100.0 ;big ship speed velocity vector (needs y speed to dock)
  $Rotation time:               69, 79, 58
  $Rear Velocity:               0.0
  $Forward accel:               20.0 ;big ship accel
  $Forward decel:               0.0 ;big ship decel, follows wp to move
  $Ship Death Effect:           PE_Explosion_Ship_Big_Imperial
  $Default PBanks:              ()
  $Default SBanks:              ()
  $SBank Capacity:              ()
  $Shields:                     12600
    ;+Auto Spread: 20
    ;+Spread From LOD: 2
  $Shield Regeneration Rate:    0.00 ;captial ship shield regen
  +Shield Regen Hit Delay:      4.0  ;captial ship shield delay
  $Max Oclk Speed:              100.0 ;big ship velocity max speed
  $Max Weapon Eng:              100.0
  $Hitpoints:                   60000 
