$Template:	Nebulon-B Template
  +Use Template:                Common Frigate Template
  $Display Name:                Nebulon-B Frigate
  $Short name:                  Nebulon-B
  $Species:                     Rebel
  +Tech Title:                  XSTR("EF76-class Nebulon-B Frigate", 954)
  +Tech Description:
  XSTR("Also known as the Nebulon-B, the EF76 Escort Frigate has been an important mainstay of the Rebel Alliance Fleet throughout the Galactic Civil War.  Wanting to directly support the fight against the Empire without drawing unwanted attention to themselves, Corellian engineers purportedly built a civilian heavy transport, but deliberately and extensively over-engineered the original specifications.  The Nebulon-B is among the largest ships built by the Corellian Engineering Corporation, and its modular design is easily refitted for military use--where it fills an important gap in the Rebellion between the nimble Corvettes and larger but far more expensive Calamari cruisers, and performs admirably alongside purpose-built capital ships.

  While the frigate is often deployed protecting transport convoys from Imperial attacks or pirate raids, many individual ships have seen further customization for a variety of specialized roles.  The Nebulon-B has seen use in command and control, long-range scouting, anti-starfighter, and medical roles.

  In its most common configuration, the Nebulon-B bristles with point-defense turrets covering every attack angle, as well as numerous heavy turbolasers allowing the frigate to go head-to-head with much larger starships.  Despite its obvious weak spots, it has proven to be a versatile and capable warship in battle and remains popular with its crews and commanders.", 955)
  $end_multi_text
  $POF file:                    nebulon-b.pof
  $POF target LOD:              1
  $Detail distance:             (0, 2000, 8000)
  $Collision LOD:               1
  $Damp:                        0.6  ; big ship damp
  $Rotdamp:                     1.0 ; big ship rot damp	
  $Max Velocity:                0.0, 5.0, 100.0 ;big ship speed velocity vector (needs y speed to dock)
  $Rotation time:               68, 78, 58
  $Rear Velocity:               0.0
  $Forward accel:               20.0 ;big ship accel
  $Forward decel:               0.0 ;big ship decel, follows wp to move
