;;=========================================================================

;; ========================================================================
;;                  Vindicator and Interdictor
$Template:	Vindicator Template
  +Use Template:                Common CruiserMedium Template
  $Display Name:                Vindicator Cruiser
  $Short name:                  Vindicator
  $Species:                     Imperial
  +Tech Title:                  XSTR("Vindicator-class Heavy Cruiser", 964)
  +Tech Description:
  XSTR("Designed and built by Sienar Fleet Systems to phase out the aging Dreadnaught-class, the Vindicator-class heavy cruiser has emerged as an integral component of the Imperial Starfleet.  In the early years of the New Order, the Imperial Navy relied heavily on Dreadnaught-class cruisers to carry out duties for which a Star Destroyer would be excessive.  Though robust, the centuries-old vessels had hardly been built with modern Imperial standards in mind.  Many contractors recognized the potential for a lucrative contract and lobbied for the Imperial Senate to commission a new line of heavy cruisers.  Leveraging their impressive reputation born of the renowned TIE series, Sienar Fleet Systems ultimately beat out its competitors and secured the valuable Imperial contract.  

  Designed in accordance with Navy doctrine, the Vindicator-class provides a number of improvements over the similarly-sized Dreadnaught class.  Newer engine components provide improved turning and acceleration, while the ship's cutting-edge armored plating is both stronger and lighter than that of the Dreadnaught.  Cargo and hangar bays are optimized for rapid deployment of TIEs and troop transports, which allows the Vindicator to swiftly counter insurgent activity on the ground or in space.  The long-range sensors and communications systems are particularly powerful for a warship of this size.  In addition, of course, the Vindicator benefits from modern shipboard automation, leaving its crew much leaner than that of the Dreadnaught.

  Despite all these capabilities, some drawbacks persist.  The ship's systems are highly complex, which necessarily impacts repair speed.  To make matters worse, Sienar deliberately built many of the Vindicator's bespoke components to be difficult for its competitors to replicate--which means that a damaged Vindicator can only be fully repaired at a Sienar dockyard equipped with proprietary manufacturing machinery.  Furthermore, engagements with Rebel starfighters have revealed that the ventral hull can be alarmingly vulnerable to fighter attack, which has increased the minimum number of TIE squadrons required for deployment with the Vindicator.  Nevertheless, the Vindicator is a highly capable heavy cruiser, and the number of hulls in Navy service continues to increase.", 965)
  $end_multi_text
  $POF file:                    vindicator.pof
  $POF target LOD:              1
  $Detail distance:             (0, 2000, 4000, 8500)
  $Collision LOD:               1
  $Damp:                        0.6 ; big ship damp 
  $Rotdamp:                     1.0 ; big ship rot damp	
  $Max Velocity:                0.0, 5.0, 100.0 ;big ship speed velocity vector (needs y speed to dock)
  $Rotation time:               86, 99, 73
