$Template:	Interdictor Template
  +Use Template:                Common CruiserMedium Template
  $Display Name:                Interdictor Cruiser
  $Short name:                  Interdictor
  $Species:                     Imperial
  +Tech Title:                  XSTR("Interdictor-class Cruiser", 966)
  +Tech Description:
  XSTR("A support ship built for a highly specialized role, the Interdictor-class cruiser represents a dramatic advance in space combat technology.  In the early years of the New Order, resistant governments in numerous systems attempted to challenge the Empire from their home territories, but were no match for the Empire's industrial capacity.  As the years progressed and insurgent cells became more connected, Rebels began performing hit-and-run raids from across the Galaxy, resulting in increased difficulty in capturing fleeing targets and, thereby, locating enemy bases of operations.  Eager to draw further from the Empire's bottomless pocketbook, Sienar Fleet Systems capitalized on their close relationship with the Imperial Navy and secured a contract to design and build a ship capable of blocking hyperspace escapes by using artificial gravity wells.  Building on the existing Vindicator hull, engineers at Sienar worked to strengthen the frame to support four large gravity well generators.  To accommodate these changes, the hangar was shortened, long-range sensor capabilities were reduced, and much of the ship's power was diverted to the gravity wells, resulting in slightly weaker shields and a far less potent turbolaser armament.  

  Though the ship is ill-suited to one-on-one engagements, the worth of the new Interdictor-class cruiser to Imperial operations cannot be overstated.  The presence of an Interdictor renders the basic tactic of retreat entirely unavailable, as the four gravity well generators can prevent any ships, small or large, from making the jump to lightspeed.  Early deployments in the Atollon system were a great surprise to Rebel forces, and continued use across the Galaxy has resulted in the capture or destruction of countless hostile vessels that would have otherwise escaped.  Engagements against well-armed hostile forces did reveal that the destruction of even one of the gravity generators triggered a chain reaction that destroyed the entire vessel.  Thus, Interdictor-class cruisers are best deployed in circumstances where fire superiority is already assured, and constant protection from both TIE screens and dedicated warships is an absolute necessity.  Furthermore--and unsurprisingly, given the cutting-edge nature of this vessel--the Interdictor's critical components require precision engineering to a standard entirely beyond the capacity of most manufacturers, sharply limiting the speed of both repair and production.  Even with these drawbacks, and the class's limited numbers, the Interdictor continues to inspire awe in the Empire's faithful--and dread in its enemies.  ", 967)
  $end_multi_text
  $POF file:                    interdictor.pof
