;;=========================================================================

;; ========================================================================
;;                   			  ISD
$Template:	Star Destroyer Template
  +Use Template:                Common CruiserLarge Template
  $Display Name:                Imperial Star Destroyer ;;II-class is too long
  $Short name:                  Star Destroyer
  $Species:                     Imperial
  +Tech Title:                  XSTR("Imperial-class Star Destroyer", 970) ;;II-class is too long
  +Tech Description:
  XSTR("A decade after the end of the Clone Wars, the Imperial Navy began an extensive modernization effort to reduce costs and expand its considerable presence in the Outer Rim.  The most expensive and obvious target for streamlining was the mainstay of the fleet, the Imperator Star Destroyer.  The original Imperator was very much a product of rushed wartime necessity, with a 'make it work' philosophy in evidence throughout its design.  Naturally, it had been built with virtually no regard for future refitting.  Though many candidates were considered to replace the Imperator, in the end, Kuat's own redesign was selected and the Imperial-I and II programs were launched.  The Imperial I-class (those ships previously designated as Imperator) would receive upgrades to their holonet transmitters, deflector shields, and certain other systems, but were to be gradually phased out of production as dry-docks retooled for Imperial-II production.

  The II-class (or ImpStar Deuce, as spacers prefer to call it) features small but significant improvements over its predecessor in almost every regard.  While the class mounts the same KDY Destroyer-I ion engines that propelled the Imperator, the new reactor pushes the engines to their limits, increasing speed considerably.  Shield strength has been marginally improved, the hull has been reinforced using knowledge gleaned from years of experience with the Tector class, and the primary armament has been upgraded from antiquated ultra-heavy Clone-Wars era dual turbolaser batteries to far more efficient modern octuple turrets--lethal in ship-to-ship combat, and well-optimized for orbital bombardment.  The fighter launch systems have been streamlined for faster combat deployment, and where the Imperator's ground-assault capabilities were an afterthought, the Imperial-II was built for the task, with dedicated bays capable of carrying and deploying a full mechanized division.  Most critically of all, these new Star Destroyers have been designed with likely future developments in mind, meaning the gap between the I and II classes will only continue to grow as newer and better technologies are developed for this, the Empire's premier warship.", 971)
  $end_multi_text
  $POF file:                    isd.pof
