$Template:	Fondor Full Template
  +Use Template:                Common Station Template
  $Display Name:                Golan Station
  $Short name:                  Golan Station
  $Species:                     Imperial
  +Tech Title:                  XSTR("Golan D-class Station", 984)
  +Tech Description:
  XSTR("The Empire's massive proliferation of multi-kilometer warships demands shipbuilding and repair yards on a scale rarely before seen--and they must be well-protected, for if the maintenance of Star Destroyers in a given area were to become impossible, the Empire's security would swiftly collapse.  The D-class, built by Golan Arms on commission from the Imperial Navy, exists to meet that need.

  Designed to withstand large-scale assaults, D-class stations possess long-range and short-range turbolaser batteries and boast the strongest armor rating of any installation in this size range.  In addition, the modularity of the station design allows for multiple configurations depending on specific needs.  The most common configuration can repair and dock two Star Destroyers while simultaneously being able to rapidly deploy dozens of TIEs from four flanking hangars.  Furthermore, this setup provides two small complementary hangars for additional TIEs or sets of repair droids, a central hangar for high-ranking Imperial personnel, and an extended covered hangar that can house ships up to six hundred meters in length, including Dreadnaught-class or Vindicator-class heavy cruisers.

 While the extreme durability of the D-class renders it even more expensive than it would otherwise be, it ensures that these installations are rarely at risk of destruction by enemy forces.  Documented attacks usually revolve around hit-and-run strikes against moored capital ships that are undergoing repairs.  To minimize these vulnerabilities, the stations require a large fighter complement and an even larger crew, raising costs yet further.  But for the Empire, there is little choice: only a facility as large and secure as the D-class can support its vast infrastructure.", 985)
  $end_multi_text
