$Template:	Shield Gate Template
  +Use Template:                Common Station Template
  $Display Name:                Golan Shield Gate
  $Short name:                  Shield Gate
  $Species:                     Imperial
  +Tech Title:                  XSTR("Golan M-class Shield Gate", 986)
  +Tech Description:
  XSTR("Leveraging the modular design framework established by the very successful Golan station series, the Golan M-class Shield Gate is among the most durable and highly specialized mass-produced orbital installations in the Galaxy.  Planetary shields are one of the best ways to safeguard terrestrial bases and populations, but conventionally such defenses require manually deactivating the entire shield to let craft pass through.  Shield-wide shutoffs quickly become a liability on busy worlds, since the frequent shield deactivations necessitated by regular traffic present windows for non-authorized craft--anywhere across the planet--to bypass the shield.
  
  A shield gate solves this problem by using an array of inverted deflectors to create a narrow gap in the shield.  This strategy allows the vast majority of the shield to remain active while allowing a stream of craft to pass through the small gate port, which, being of manageable size, is easy to guard.  Naturally, this bottleneck sometimes results in long ship queues, but most parties concerned enough with security to install a planetary shield consider the ability to scan and vet each ship coming through the gate well worth the tradeoff.
  
  Being a shield gate built for military use, the M-class is armed and armored to a standard suitable for engagements with hostile capital ships up to destroyer scale.  Further protection is provided by the station's two voluminous hangar bays, each capable of deploying multiple full squadrons in seconds.  In case of emergency, the M-class has a rapid-shutoff feature which quickly closes the gate prevent unwanted ships from entering or exiting the shielded region.
  
  When the shield is fully closed, all communication between the planet and space is blocked, unless it is transmitted through the station itself.", 987)
  $end_multi_text
  $POF file:                    fondor_shield_gate.pof
